% ==============================================================================
% Operand Stack Manipulation Primitives in PostScript
% Tests dup, exch, pop, index, copy, roll, count, and custom stack procedures.
% ==============================================================================

% 1. Test dup, exch, and pop
10 20 exch       % stack: 20 10
dup              % stack: 20 10 10
pop              % stack: 20 10

% 2. Push additional items
30 40 50         % stack bottom-to-top: 20, 10, 30, 40, 50

% Test index: 0-index is 50, 2-index into [50, 50, ...] is 40, 4-index is 30
0 index          % 50
2 index          % 40
4 index          % 30
add add          % 30 + 40 + 50 = 120 -> stack top is 120

% 3. Test copy (duplicate top 2 items: 50, 120)
2 copy           % duplicates [120, 50] -> stack top has 50 120
add              % 50 + 120 = 170

% 4. Test roll
% Stack top 3 items are: [170, 120, 50]
3 1 roll         % cyclically shift top 3: [120, 50, 170]
3 -1 roll        % reverse cyclical shift: [170, 120, 50]

% 5. Test procedure with stack ops: reverse top 3 elements
/reverse3 {
    3 1 roll
    exch
} def

reverse3         % [170, 120, 50] -> [50, 120, 170]

% Sum the reversed top 3 items: 50 + 120 + 170 = 340
add add

% 6. Test count: remaining items on stack are 20, 10, 30, 40, 340 (total 5 items)
count

% Final operand stack top to bottom:
% [5, 340, 40, 30, 10, 20]
